{"author":{"id":"dec876858d28babbadcead4137861bf586626b8518cbce9c5f4fc52ac3b424b8"},"ops":[{"type":1,"timestamp":1794165763,"nonce":"5v5VKL8084o8omaJ5piULm1eoO8=","title":"Incremental update drops class-selector styles after VisualOnly and LayoutChanged (GitHub issue 70, PR 71)","message":"Reported at https://github.com/project-blinc/Blinc/issues/70, fix proposed in https://github.com/project-blinc/Blinc/pull/71 (not merged).\n\nDefect: the desktop runner's \"Normal incremental update\" branch in windowed/event_loop/frame/rebuild.rs re-applies class-selector styles only after ChildrenChanged. incremental_update replaces node props in place with the new tree's props, which carry no class styles, so after VisualOnly or LayoutChanged every node that took its background, colour or font from a class rule is drawn with defaults. The window goes black until a hover re-resolves the hovered element.\n\nChecked here: with only PR 71's rebuild.rs change applied to main, its three tests pass (class_background_survives_a_visual_only_update, class_background_survives_a_layout_changed_update, incremental_update_alone_drops_the_class_background). The third shows the defect without the call. The change was applied temporarily and reverted; nothing from the PR is in the working tree.\n\nReview notes for PR 71:\n- Ordering matches the ChildrenChanged arm (base styles, layout overrides, then layout), and NoChanges does nothing.\n- Cost. apply_stylesheet_base_styles is a whole-tree pass, and VisualOnly is the usual result of a signal-driven update, so it now runs on every visual update. A whole-tree style pass per frame was 75% of the iPhone example's idle CPU (a different pass, apply_stylesheet_state_styles, selector matching with ElementRegistry::has_class). Measure on cn_demo before merging. Narrowing it to the nodes incremental_update actually replaced would keep the fix and drop the cost.\n- Same pattern elsewhere. web.rs (build_and_update arm) and the headless harness (blinc_recorder testing/headless.rs) also treat VisualOnly as a no-op. A probe in the headless harness did not show the defect: the class background stayed with and without a restyle, so the harness restyles somewhere else in its frame. The web runner was not checked.\n- iOS and Android are not affected: they rebuild the tree and call apply_all_stylesheet_styles, and do not call incremental_update.\n\nOpen: decide on the PR (merge as is, or narrow the restyle), and check the web runner.","files":null}]}